            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0140" n="66" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg66"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.002/46</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-15T14:00:00+02:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1289. Milyukov resigned, Tereshchenko appointed Minister of Foreign Affairs,
                    Kerensky appointed Minister of War. No appointment yet to Ministry of Finance or
                    Ministry [of] Justice. Kerensky and Tereshchenko both favor vigorous prosecution
                    of war. It is believed these appointments will result in coalition cabinet in
                    which workmen’s committee favor offensive warfare which it is thought will be
                    waged aggressively under reformed government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
